{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "For U1 (statebased refactor): Inline the necessary parts of cauthdsl policy-construction logic using the protos directly (e.g., common/policies.SignaturePolicyEnvelope, common/policies.SignaturePolicy) instead of importing cauthdsl and protoutil wrappers.",
    "For U2 (entities refactor): Move bccsp usage behind a small internal interface defined inside the entities package, so consumers see only the entities API; the flogging dependency is replaced by a small internal logger interface or standard library usage.",
    "For U3 and U4 (marbles02_private tutorial fixes): Treat both as a single documentation/script update in the fabric-samples repository — adding the `tr -d \\\\` workaround either inline in the export expression (U4) and as a comment in the source (U3).",
    "For U5/U6/U7/U8 (externalization): Assume a target fabric-lib-go module already exists (or is co-developed in this increment) and that the work consists of moving source files, updating import paths throughout fabric, updating go.mod (replace directives during transition) and re-pointing the Go SDK to consume the externalized copy.",
    "Sequential, single-developer execution is assumed — the estimate is pure effort, not calendar duration; no parallelization of refactor/externalization work is credited.",
    "For all externalized packages, treat go module versioning and a one-shot API stability pass as part of the activity (no separate versioning spike activity).",
    "For refactor activities, include updating existing unit tests plus adding new tests for the inlined logic; no separate 'test design' activity is carved out."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "One developer performs all work, working 8-hour days, full-time on this increment.",
    "Developer already has working knowledge of the Hyperledger Fabric codebase, Go modules, and protos.",
    "The fabric-lib-go module exists and can be contributed to without lengthy cross-team coordination.",
    "No backward-compatibility shim is required inside fabric after externalization (callers inside fabric are updated in the same change set).",
    "The Go SDK side of U5/U6/U7/U8 is out of scope; the deliverable is the externalized package plus updated fabric consumers.",
    "The two marble tutorial user stories (U3, U4) are treated as a small, single documentation/script edit; their effort is additive because they are listed as separate stories.",
    "8-hour workday is the unit of effort; fractional days are used for small activities.",
    "Standard unit + integration test execution is included in each refactor/externalization activity; no separate 'testing' activity beyond a final integration validation pass."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "U1 — Refactor statebased package to remove fabric/comm, fabric/protoutil and pkg/errors deps",
      "activity_description": "Analyse every use of cauthdsl and protoutil in core/chaincode/shim/ext/statebased. Inline the needed SignaturePolicy / collection-config helpers using the protos packages directly. Replace pkg/errors with stdlib errors (or fmt.Errorf with %w). Update unit tests, run go list to confirm only protos packages remain as fabric imports, and verify chaincode examples that use the statebased builder still build and behave correctly.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U2 — Refactor entities package to remove bccsp and flogging deps",
      "activity_description": "Introduce a small crypto-provider interface inside core/chaincode/shim/ext/entities (e.g., KeyProvider, HashProvider) that mirrors the small surface of bccsp actually used. Replace direct bccsp calls with calls through that interface. Replace flogging with an internal lightweight logger (or an injected logger interface). Update the existing encryption tests, add new unit tests, and verify go list reports no bccsp/flogging imports from the entities package.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U3 — Document/fix marbles02_private JSON parsing workaround (comment in chaincode source)",
      "activity_description": "Update the marbles02_private.go chaincode in fabric-samples to include an explanatory comment about wrapping the MARBLE export with `tr -d \\\\` on systems (e.g., Windows-hosted shells piping into Linux VMs) where stray backslashes break JSON parsing. Re-run the tutorial end-to-end to confirm no regression.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U4 — Patch marbles02_private tutorial shell commands to use `tr -d \\\\`",
      "activity_description": "Update the README / shell script in fabric-samples for marbles02_private so the MARBLE export expression pipes through `base64 | tr -d \\\\`, preventing the JSON parsing error. Re-execute the tutorial to confirm the workaround is now applied automatically rather than only documented.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U5 — Externalize protoutil into fabric-lib-go",
      "activity_description": "Move the contents of fabric/protoutil into a new package in fabric-lib-go (e.g., github.com/hyperledger/fabric-lib-go/protoutil), adjusting imports to the new protos location. Update every internal fabric import of fabric/protoutil to the externalized path, refresh go.mod (replace directive if needed), and rerun the fabric unit and integration test suites that depend on protoutil helpers.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U6 — Externalize BCCSP into fabric-lib-go",
      "activity_description": "Move fabric/bccsp (and its subpackages: factory, sw, idemix, signer, utils, handlers, bridge) into fabric-lib-go. Rewire all internal fabric references from github.com/hyperledger/fabric/bccsp/... to the new fabric-lib-go path. Update go.mod, bccsp factory configuration loading, and unit tests for bccsp (sw, idemix). Verify the SDK copy can now consume the externalized BCCSP without vendoring modifications.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U7 — Externalize MSP into fabric-lib-go",
      "activity_description": "Move fabric/msp (and the identity helpers in internal/pkg/identity) into fabric-lib-go. Update all internal fabric references, including those in core, common, peer, and orderer packages, to the new import path. Adjust interfaces, msp-manager implementations, and identity serialization to use the externalized protos. Update msp unit tests (id, msp mgr, idemix-based MSP) and run the full identity-related integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U8 — Externalize discovery client into fabric-lib-go",
      "activity_description": "Move fabric/discovery (gossip discovery, proto, support, api) into fabric-lib-go. Update internal fabric callers (peer, gossip, comm) to the new import path. Re-run discovery-related unit tests and a small end-to-end scenario (gossip + endorsement discovery) to confirm the externalized client behaves identically.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Integration testing and validation across all changes",
      "activity_description": "Run go list to verify the dependency-clean goals for U1 and U2 are met. Build the full fabric tree against the externalized fabric-lib-go packages. Run end-to-end sample-network tests (including the marbles02_private tutorial fixes) and fix any regressions introduced by the refactors and externalizations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Documentation, code review pass, and cleanup",
      "activity_description": "Update package-level Go doc comments for refactored/externalized packages, update fabric docs that mention internal paths, and perform a self-review pass to remove dead code, fix lint warnings, and finalize the change set.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 42.0
  }
}
